Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: gate new gadgets and release bandwidth after stop

Publish the requested USB role under the worker mutex before queueing
the mode change. Apply that role to a newly created gadget and gate soft
connect until DEVICE is requested.

Hardware: delayed HOST-to-NONE registration must never pull up; then
verify NCM and hub recovery.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -277,6 +277,9 @@
 		ret = dwc3_gadget_init(dwc);
 		if (ret)
 			dev_err(dwc->dev, "failed to initialize peripheral\n");
+		else if (dwc->role_vbus_gated)
+			usb_udc_vbus_handler(dwc->gadget,
+				READ_ONCE(dwc->requested_role) == USB_ROLE_DEVICE);
 		break;
 	case DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_OTG:
 		dwc3_otg_init(dwc);
